        "original_id": "801f8189-b977-5b79-93a6-20c04bdda3d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Street Survivors\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd\n- People: Steve Gaines, Ronnie Van Zant, Allen Collins, Cassie Gaines\n- Topics: Southern rock\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Gaines was born on September 14, 1949, and died on October 20, 1977.\n- Steve Gaines was an American musician.\n- Steve Gaines was a guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for Lynyrd Skynyrd from May 11, 1976 until his death on October 20, 1977.\n- Cassie Gaines was Steve Gaines's younger sister and a backup vocalist for Lynyrd Skynyrd's live performances.\n- Lynyrd Skynyrd released Street Survivors, its fifth studio album, on October 17, 1977.\n- Street Survivors was the last Lynyrd Skynyrd album recorded by original members Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- Street Survivors was the only Lynyrd Skynyrd studio recording featuring Steve Gaines.",
